<h2>Wednesday, May 19,  2004</h2>	
<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-10"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/index.php?p=10" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Communication">Communication</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">posted by: Mark @ 11:24 pm </div>
	
	<div class="storycontent">
			<p>Ever feel like you have something to say, but you just don&#8217;t know how to put it into words.  This seems to be happening to more and more every day.  Someone will say something or do something that doesn&#8217;t sit right within my spirit and when I try to verbalize it I&#8217;m given blank stares.  Sometime&#8217;s it is funny, other times it&#8217;s just frustrating.  Actually, come to think of it, this happens to me when I&#8217;m speaking with God as well.  My spirit will be overcome with some sort of emotion or my mind will have a certain thought, but I&#8217;m unable to translate it into words.  It reminds me of this verse in the Bible:</p>
	<p><em>&#8220;In the same way the Spirit also helps our weakness; for we do not know how to pray as we should, but the Spirit Himself intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words; &#8220;</em> (Romans 8:26, NASB95) </p>
	<p>Let me tell you, these &#8220;groanings&#8221; are not fun, if that is indeed what I&#8217;ve been experiencing.
</p>
